      "name": "core.openwop.workflows.crm-ops",
      "version": "1.8.0",
      "description": "Governed CRM write-verb workflows (RFC 0013, ADR 0208 §2, ADR 0252). Where vendor.openwop-app.crm.agents.sales-ops is read-mostly (plus two assistive writes), these chains carry the riskier CRM mutations — owner assignment off a new-lead event, stale-deal follow-up, the scheduler-fired Gmail inbox sync, and contact triage (the CRM toggle variant's scoring, recorded on the contact — ADR 0837 D7) — with a human in the loop where the ADR calls for one. All tenant-specific values are run parameters (replay-deterministic). Resolves on hosts that ship the feature.crm feature + node pack (the OpenWOP reference app).",
